  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rufescens Mx Ii</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The coastal lagoons in the Gulf of Mexico and Pacific Ocean are facing pressure from fishing, tourism and livestock grazing, which has negatively impacted the wintering grounds of the reddish egret. This project will establish a long-term conservation agreement for the protection of reddish egret in Baja California Sur; acquire, reforest and restore mangrove habitat; develop a management plan for wetlands adjacent to the Laguna Ojo de Liebre; monitor reddish egret populations and their habitat; create a Conservation Business Plan for the reddish egret in Mexico; and develop outreach and community education in areas where human disturbance has been identified as a major threat.</narrative>
  </description>
